shadowfetch-ember (2.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: the Ember Mode engine for Shadowfetch Linux 2.1.2
    "Fire Edition".
  * One switch, one promise: emberd holds the 'performance' power profile
    via power-profiles-daemon (HoldProfile), falls back to the cpupower
    governor where no ppd performance profile exists, pauses a curated
    read-only list of background services behind gate conditions
    (PackageKit only when the package system is idle, ModemManager never
    when a WWAN bearer is the default route), and applies a runtime
    CPUWeight=40 drop-in to system.slice. The IOWeight claim from the
    design was dropped, not shipped as a placebo: io.weight is a no-op on
    default NVMe schedulers.
  * Always returns to Balanced, four independent ways: the ppd hold dies
    with the daemon's bus connection; /usr/libexec/ember-restore
    (idempotent, POSIX sh) undoes every mutation recorded in
    /run/shadowfetch/ember.state as ExecStartPre AND ExecStopPost; a
    ProfileReleased watch treats a profile change in the Plasma applet as
    a graceful extinguish, never a re-hold; and every mutation is
    --runtime/tmpfs, so a power cut reverts by reboot. WatchdogSec=15
    catches hangs in the engine itself.
  * emberd has NO sampler (judge must-fix folded): firewatchd is the
    single sensor source. The idle watchdog consumes the WORK-ONLY
    effective-load terms from org.shadowfetch.Firewatch1 -- thermal
    proximity is excluded from the auto-return test, so a hot thin laptop
    cannot pin itself into Ember forever (that term stays in the flame
    display, which Firewatch owns).
  * Read-only status on the system bus: com.shadowfetch.Ember1 with
    {armed, hold_active, paused_units, state_file_hash}.
  * The active local console user flips the switch without a password
    (polkit rules file, scoped to exactly this unit and the
    start/stop/restart verbs).
  * Ships the pkexec ember-duration helper -- the single root-write path
    for the RuntimeMaxSec time limit and the /run/shadowfetch/ember-profile
    app-profile marker (IA fold: session QML never writes root paths;
    ember-restore clears the marker in the same pass).

 -- Shadowfetch Project <signing@shadowfetch.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:30:00 -0400
